# The operator's own live config at the repo root — NOT the committed examples/ template.
/rackctl.yaml

# Local planning notes.
#
# Org-wide convention (nanohype/CLAUDE.md): a repo holds shipped artifacts, not working
# notes. Campaign status, audit grades and remediation ledgers never live in a repo — a
# committed record of what a repo scored and how it got fixed is exactly the accretion
# evidence the greenfield doctrine exists to prevent. Every other org repo ignores this
# path; rackctl did not, and had three plan files tracked. They now live outside the repo
# with the rest of the corpus.
.plans/
